<p>The BBC says it plans to cut about 1,800 to 2,000 jobs over the next two years, roughly one in 10 roles at the British public broadcaster. Acting director-general Rhodri Talfan Davies announced the move, saying the broadcaster is under significant financial pressure and needs to respond quickly. The cuts are part of a broader push to lower operating costs and shore up the BBC’s finances as the media industry changes and pressure grows on its funding model. The decision marks another round of restructuring at one of the world’s most influential news and cultural institutions, which says 94% of UK adults still use its services each month.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/kUMT7VeoZ203qbTbrhMKsgPW5TN-AB1LQF1eSIs2IVLc4X3fFlXMoWQKhtsg-QlCP4YgbRfmIXqJ7BMRze7vdh3KIyTuJY_Km42_Viso50fzdNu8ghFv3fXOzt6GgLg0gl0MmCbMS1LLkNesEoKWdeVUFCZt9oeQJL234PoSLKsFRw' alt='The headquarters of the British Broadcasting Corporation in London.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Budget target: The BBC said earlier this year that it wanted to cut about a tenth of its budget by 2029, and the new layoffs are meant to help deliver that plan.</li><li>Savings goal: Euronews reported that the restructuring is meant to save €575 million in operating costs over two years.</li><li>Biggest drive: SCMP called the move the BBC’s biggest redundancy programme in 15 years.</li><li>Employee base: The broadcaster has about 21,500 employees, underscoring the scale of the organisation making the cuts.</li></ul><blockquote>While we still have to work through the detail, we anticipate the overall number of jobs will fall by 1,800-2,000 - Rhodri Talfan Davies</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Rhodri Talfan Davies: The acting director-general stressed the urgency, telling staff the BBC had to respond &quot;at pace&quot; to significant financial pressure as it works through the details of the cuts. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/economy/article/2026/04/15/bbc-announces-up-to-2-000-layoffs-in-next-two-years_6752465_19.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>BBC management: The corporation had already warned earlier this year of &quot;substantial financial pressures,&quot; so management is framing the redundancies as part of a broader response to strain that has been building rather than a sudden shift. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/bbc-will-cut-up-to-2-000-jobs-to-save-10-of-its-budget-over-2-years-11364495#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Coverage across outlets: Reports framed the decision as a sign that even a major public broadcaster is not shielded from the financial pressure hitting legacy media organisations. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/15/world/europe/bbc-job-cuts.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/15/world/europe/bbc-job-cuts.html'>BBC Announces Plan to Cut Around 2,000 Jobs</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3350235/bbc-slash-2000-jobs-biggest-redundancy-drive-15-years'>BBC to slash 2,000 jobs in biggest redundancy drive in 15 years</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/economy/article/2026/04/15/bbc-announces-up-to-2-000-layoffs-in-next-two-years_6752465_19.html'>BBC announces up to 2,000 layoffs in next two years</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/bbc-will-cut-up-to-2-000-jobs-to-save-10-of-its-budget-over-2-years-11364495#publisher=newsstand'>BBC Will Cut Up To 2,000 Jobs To Save 10% Of Its Budget Over 2 Years</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/15/bbc-to-cut-up-to-2000-jobs-in-next-two-years-to-save-575ml-from-operating-costs'>BBC to cut up to 2,000 jobs in next two years to save €575ml from operating costs</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/bbc-to-cut-up-to-2000-jobs-major-cost-saving-move-1236722352/'>The BBC announces that it will cut between 1,800 and 2,000 jobs, around 1-in-10 employees, citing the need to address &quot;significant financial pressures&quot;.</a> - variety.com</li></ul>